# Findings accepted on purpose. Read by Trivy in scan-images.yml and ci.yml.
# Give every entry a reason and an expiry date (exp:YYYY-MM-DD), so the scan
# reports it again if the cause hasn't been fixed by then.

# guava DoS during deserialization (CVE-2026-102554), bundled in planetiler.jar.
# Not reachable: planetiler never deserializes Java objects.
# Fixed in guava 33.7.2. Upstream planetiler is on 33.7.1 and its Dependabot
# will bump it; then move the fork's head up and delete this entry.
CVE-2026-102554 exp:2026-12-31

# jackson-core DoS on malformed JSON (CVE-2026-89407, CVE-2026-89425), in the
# copy Apache Parquet shades into planetiler.jar (shaded/parquet/…, from
# parquet-jackson 1.18.1). Planetiler's own jackson-core is 2.23.0 and not
# affected. Probably not reachable: Parquet metadata is Thrift, and GeoParquet's
# JSON is parsed by planetiler's own Jackson. Fixed in parquet-floor 2.5
# (Parquet 1.18.2, Jackson 2.22.4); upstream planetiler is on parquet-floor 2.3.
# Once it bumps, move the fork's head up and delete these entries.
CVE-2026-89407 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-89425 exp:2026-12-31
